00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.000
A man: I, I, I (unintelligible)

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: The more... Yes. A man: (unintelligible)

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: The more knowledge they acquire,

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.000
the more, I mean, they're just about to prohibit alcohol, for example.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:34.000
And here's a drunk captain who polluted Alaska because of alcohol.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.000
The whole country knows the evils of alcohol.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:40.000
So, when they look at the Quran, they see alcohol is prohibited.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.000
It matches the common sense. It matches their knowledge.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:51.000
I mean, this man had a ten mile wide channel.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:58.000
They said a child can maneuver this super tanker through those ten miles.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: But, but he's not, he's not even a child. I mean, he's passed out.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:08.000
A woman: Yeah, (unintelligible). I wanna just say (unintelligible). So, he wasn't drunk.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: I bet you the crew was drunk, also.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:15.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: I think it takes a clever captain to hit those rocks.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.000
A man: Either that or (unintelligible) for it.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.000
A man: Excuse to make it right.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.000
A man: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, they wouldn't do that, you know. No. The guy, the guy was drunk, you know.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:33.000
So, what I'm saying is that the more knowledge the human being acquires, the closer they get to God's laws

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: on their own.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:43.000
Hamid: Aren't you gonna go as far as getting the advice of the judges because after all we are humans.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:52.000
And when it comes to dividing your own wealth, you may, it will be better (unintelligible).

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:59.000
So, I just listen to you and (unintelligible).

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:07.000
If someone has to pass a judgment on the wealth of a guy, if it's left up to the, to the, the first man,

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:13.000
which is, which soon (unintelligible) very wealthy,

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:18.000
if someone has to step in and the wife brings the checkbook,

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.000
(unintelligible)

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.000
Hamid: what do you think this could mean? I mean,...

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, remember that the believers' affairs are decided by consultation. We're talking about believers.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:36.000
If they're believers, they will be fair, and they will consult, and they will, they will maintain...

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:42.000
Again, in Sura 4, like Lori mentioned, they emphasize, God emphasizes the amicable relations.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:48.000
So, a husband and wife didn't get along together and decided to part. They don't have to be enemies.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:52.000
In fact, God says, do not, you must maintain the amicable relations among you."

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, there'll be mutual consultation and mutual contentment.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.000
Hamid: But realistically, you mentioned about alcohol.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.000
Hamid: Yeah, it shouldn't be there. It should be prohibited.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:14.000
Hamid: But, but the, Ok, the reality, I'm talking about, you know, nowadays life. I'm, I'm just imagining the (unintelligible)

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hamid, you're hung up on the time of applicability of the Quran.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: The Quran is applicable through any time,

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: till the end of the world. Not nowadays. Hamid: No, but (unintelligible)

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.000
Hamid: Are you, are you saying we, we do not need Islamic judges?

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:33.000
Hamid: Is that, is that the content of the, of my argument is this, should we go to Istanbul?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, actually, we do need Islamic judges. I didn't say that. Yeah.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because the general public will not be as familiar with the Quran as, as they should be, or as they need to be.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Hamid: I thought that...

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the Islamic judges are needed.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:53.000
I hit somebody's car, and then so how much do I compensate that person?

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Then, we both go to the Islamic judge, and the person whose car I hit,

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:03.000
he will say "this cost me $800 to fix, and I lost 8 hours of work, and this and this."

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: Then, the judge will calculate that, and will tell me to compensate the person.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Hamid: I thought you said that if we are a believer, which is (unintelligible) by writing a check.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: You'll do that, too. But then, if there is, you know, remember the judge is needed when there is dispute.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:23.000
The judge is needed when there is dispute. If the person knows what he's doing, you don't need a judge.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:27.000
Maximum freedom is guaranteed in the Quran, also.

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: Let's go to 66 and Lori. Anybody is saying something?

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:35.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: 66.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.000
Lori: Verse 1.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:53.000
[66:1] O you prophet, why do you prohibit what GOD has made lawful for you, just to please your wives? GOD is Forgiver, Merciful.*

00:22:54.000 --> 00:23:00.000
[66:2] GOD has decreed for you the laws dealing with your oaths. GOD is your Lord, and He is the Omniscient, Most Wise.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:16.000
[66:3] The prophet had trusted some of his wives with a certain statement, then one of them spread it, and GOD let him know about it. He then informed his wife of part of the issue, and disregarded part. She asked him, "Who informed you of this?" He said, "I was informed by the Omniscient, Most Cognizant."

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:28.000
[66:4] If the two of you repent to GOD, then your hearts have listened. But if you band together against him, then GOD is his ally, and so is Gabriel and the righteous believers. Also, the angels are his helpers.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:43.000
[66:5] If he divorces you, GOD will substitute other wives in your place who are better than you; submitters (Muslims), believers (Mu'mins), obedient, repentant, worshipers, pious, either previously married, or virgins.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:56.000
[66:6] O you who believe, protect yourselves and your families from the Hellfire whose fuel is people and rocks. Guarding it are stern and powerful angels who never disobey GOD; they do whatever they are commanded to do.

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:03.000
[66:7] O you who disbelieved, do not apologize today. You are being requited only for what you did.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:08.000
In the first verse of (unintelligible) footnote,

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:12.000
it says that Mohammedans around the world believe that Muhammad was infallible.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:16.000
This verse teaches us that he was indeed a fallible human being.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:22.000
And there are a number of verses cited that will back this up.

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:31.000
The messenger is given the responsibility to deliver the messages, and when he does that, he is

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:38.000
in accordance with God's laws and those things are preserved.

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:46.000
But the messenger is also a human being and is subject to the same test that everybody else is subject to, an even greater test, because,

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:50.000
you know, with the responsibility comes the, you know, the, the test.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:58.000
And God made it this way so that we would not worship the messenger. That's God's system.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:03.000
If the messenger was perfect, then, he would be god.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:06.000
So, it doesn't make any sense.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:11.000
The messengers are just humans. Their only job is to deliver the message, to clarify.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:16.000
They are sent as a mercy from God to give the information to the rest of us.

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.000
So, they're going to make mistakes.

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:28.000
And again, this is to weed out those who would turn away because the messenger isn't perfect. We know the history of Moses.

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:36.000
And he went to Pharaoh and Pharaoh said, you know, "why should I listen to you? You stutter. You know, you're one of our slaves."

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:42.000
Even though, we know Moses, you know, showed him all these miracles, but it didn't make any difference.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:47.000
But that was God's will. We have to believe God and now the messenger.

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:49.000
And we know what happened.

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:56.000
The Christians, you know, who worshipped Jesus because

00:25:56.000 --> 00:26:00.000
it wasn't enough that he was a messenger. They wanted to make him a god besides God.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.000
And it's the same thing with Muslims who worship Muhammad and they think that he was perfect.

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:13.000
And there are all these myths and stories and legends that, about him that don't even make any sense. He was just a man.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:20.000
And, and God is very careful in the Quran to point out his errors, too, but like Rashad said, not to scandalize him.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:25.000
I mean, God doesn't get anything from that. But to make us realize that he was a man and don't worship him. He was just a man.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:33.000
Listen to the message. It doesn't make any difference. The messengers all come with the same message, every one of them.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:40.000
And it's God's intent that they do make mistakes and they are imperfect so that we won't worship them.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:50.000
And to weed out those who will not listen to the messenger because they don't like him or they think that he's not perfect.

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:59.000
And the next verse is,

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:03.000
again there, there isn't anything. I remember from one time in one of our discussions

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:07.000
in Quranic study many, many years ago. There were some people from

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:12.000
another mosque and they were talking about the Hadith and Sunnah. The importance of it was because it was history.

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:18.000
And you know, if you, if you read the Quran, the Quran is the greatest history.

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
We know what people think.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:25.000
We know what people thought. You know, we know what they did under the tree and they, they got together and think that were in their minds.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:27.000
It's the greatest history.

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:31.000
Oh, we know here about what happened to, to his wives.

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:38.000
He just told them something and they went and spread it. I mean, so, this is God telling us this. And it's, it's a lesson for all of us.

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:46.000
And we're not supposed to be mean. We're not supposed to gossip. We're not supposed to slander.

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:51.000
We're, you know, if something is entrusted to us, we're supposed to respect that and, and take heed.

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:58.000
And you can't hide from God. You know, she asked "how did you know?" And he said "I know from God."

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:02.000
You can't get away from anything. God is Omnipotent. He's Omniscient.

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:10.000
He told in verse 4 to repent and that the messenger is, is protected against these things.

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:15.000
And even if everybody banded together against him, God is saying that

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:19.000
[66:4] ... GOD is his ally, and so are Gabriel and the righteous believers. ...

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:28.000
And as far as reasons for divorce, if he divorces you, you know, in this case because of the

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:34.000
their behavior, then God will make it up to him. He'll give him a better wife.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:40.000
You know, what we were talking about earlier is that with difficulty there is ease. And if you

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:48.000
have to suffer in some way for the cause of God, it's always made up to you. You're always rewarded because God is the Most Gracious.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:55.000
In verse 6, we're admonished to protect ourselves and our families from the Hellfire.

00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:56.000
And how do we do that?

00:28:56.000 --> 00:29:03.000
We do it by, number one, being responsible for ourselves, obeying God's laws,

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:11.000
obeying the commandments, doing, fulfilling all of our religious duties, but also think to it that our families do the same thing.

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:17.000
You know, parents have to make sure their children know how to do the Prayers,

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:21.000
make sure that the children do the Prayers when it's time for them to Fast, to make sure that they Fast.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:27.000
Spouses have to, you know, help their, help each other do the right thing.

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:33.000
We're all, we all need to help each other because we all have the same weaknesses.

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:44.000
And we're told here that once we get to the Day of Judgment, there are angels who never disobey God.

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:51.000
And every command will be carried out and nobody will have any power to do anything else.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:57.000
And on that day, we'll be told,

00:29:57.000 --> 00:30:04.000
well, God willing, not we, but those who disbelieve will be told not to apologize, that they're just being repaid for what they did.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:10.000
Again, it all comes back to us. God has given us free will. The decision was ours.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:15.000
Once we made that decision, He helped us along in whatever that decision was.

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:23.000
If we chose to disbelieve, He helped the disbelievers disbelieve. He actually leads them astray.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:25.000
If this is their decision, then He helps them in that decision.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:36.000
If we choose to believe, then He helps us in our belief. He gives us the messages, the revelations, the steps to do what we have to do.

00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:41.000
And God is, is just. We're only requited for what we did.

00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:45.000
We're not held responsible for anybody else's sins.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:48.000
A wife is not held responsible for her husband's sins.

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:56.000
You know, parents aren't held responsible for their children's sins. We have to be responsible for ourselves and everybody else...

00:30:57.000 --> 00:31:00.000
Lori: Any questions or comments on this section?

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:09.000
Hamid: How far can we go, should we go, as far as pursuing the kids,

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:12.000
(unintelligible)

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:17.000
Hamid: to, for Praying, or Fasting, or (unintelligible)?

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:23.000
Lori: Well, obviously, you can only do so much.

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:29.000
You can tell them to do it. You can set the example. You can make sure they do it up to a certain point.

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:32.000
But at some point, everybody is responsible for themselves.

00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:39.000
But, you know, if you want your children to get up and, and Pray the, the Morning Prayer,

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:43.000
and it's hard for them to do it, you might have to really work with them to do it.

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:50.000
Lori: Maybe, not allow them to have their breakfast or something until, until they had do their Morning Prayer, or, you know.

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:52.000
Hamid: They are children, and they are not responsible.

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
(unintelligible) my point is this,

00:31:54.000 --> 00:32:00.000
Hamid: If we go as far as waking them up, and lining them up and say "well, Pray."

